From 6547d41c4d6f750eb182c0abfe74691f04678d08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:15:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] feat(core): delete results say gone or pending;
 Background propagation; uid/resourceVersion preconditions (C6)

resources_delete answered "Resource deleted successfully" as soon as
the API accepted the delete, whatever was left (K8S-10): an object held
by a finalizer, a terminating Pod, a Namespace being emptied. On the
native session an agent reported a clean-up "done" while Pods were
still terminating. It also sent no propagation policy, so deleting a
Job orphaned its Pods (K8S-22, the API's default for batch/v1 Job;
kubectl defaults to Background), and no precondition, so a
read-then-delete loop could delete an object recreated in between
(K8S-04).

resources_delete now:
- reads the object again after the delete and says what is true:
  "Resource deleted successfully" when it is gone (unchanged text);
  "Resource deletion pending: ... held by finalizers <list>" or
  "... is terminating (deletionTimestamp, grace period)" when it still
  exists; and notes when an object of the same name already exists
  again with another uid;
- sends propagationPolicy Background by default, like kubectl, with an
  optional `propagationPolicy` argument (Background, Foreground,
  Orphan);
- takes optional `uid` and `resourceVersion` preconditions; a failed
  precondition is reported as such, and nothing is deleted.

pods_delete reports a Pod that is still terminating in the same way.

The resources_delete test for a Namespace expected "Resource deleted
successfully"; a Namespace is only marked for deletion until the
namespace controller has emptied it (envtest runs none), so it now
expects the pending text. The propagation and precondition fields
are checked on the request body against a mock API server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
